event: content_block_delta
data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/tmp/plan.md\", \"content\": \"Plan for mission \\\"greet, tested\\\":\\n\\n1. Dispatch to dev: implement src/greet.py with greet(name) -\u003e \\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\",\\n   and tests/test_greet.py with at least two cases (a normal name, and the empty\\n   string), such that `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exits 0. Require\\n   dev to run the tests itself before replying and commit to its own branch.\\n2. Wait for dev's reply.\\n3. Judge: fetch dev's branch, inspect src/greet.py and tests/test_greet.py,\\n   run `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` myself against the fetched tree\\n   to verify exit code 0 independently of dev's report. Check the empty-string\\n   case is actually asserted (not just present in a docstring/comment) and that\\n   greet's return format matches exactly \\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\".\\n4. Accept if all three criteria verified; otherwise send precise rework\\n   instructions naming exactly what's missing/wrong.\\n5. Once accepted, reply to mission m1 with --outcome campaign-met.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

